  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The effectiveness of the labour inspection system and of social dialogue mechanisms is strengthened</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reforming the public administration system in Moldova is a key requirement for EU accession, and the State Labour Inspectorate (SLI) requires institutional changes to effectively address labour market challenges. The ILO&#x2019;s support focuses on strengthening the SLI&#x2019;s capacity to fulfil its state control mandate and improve labour inspection effectiveness. 
The Ministry of Labour and Social Protection is leading the reform of the SLI at both the legislative and institutional levels to enhance efficiency, particularly in occupational safety and health, and the fight against undeclared work. The reform aligns with ILO Conventions No. 81 and No. 129, which Moldova ratified, as well as ILO guidelines on labour inspection and strategic compliance intervention. The institutional reform aims to increase the number and quality of inspections, enhance strategic resource allocation, develop a labour inspection case management system, promote Strategic Compliance Planning for the SLI, strengthen performance evaluation and reward mechanisms for labour inspectors, and provide training on soft skills, legal frameworks, and inspection techniques. 
The ILO is supporting the review of the 2022 labour inspection assessment to validate findings and identify opportunities for improvement. It is also assisting in updating and revising labour inspection tools, including guidelines and manuals, to better address the diverse needs and challenges faced by all workers, regardless of gender. Additionally, the ILO is working to enhance the capacities of labour inspectors by providing training on modern labour inspection procedures and international labour standards. A comprehensive Training of Trainers program is also being developed to ensure sustainable capacity-building for labour inspectors. These efforts will contribute to a more effective and responsive labour inspection system, ensuring better compliance with international standards and fostering inclusive economic growth in Moldova.</narrative>
  </description>
